/*!
    \title Qt Graphs Theme Overview
    \page qtgraphs-overview-theme.html
    \brief An overview of the theme in the Qt Graphs module.

    A theme is a built-in collection of style settings for all visual elements
    of a graph, such as colors, fonts, and visibility, and the strength of the
    light and ambient light.

    Qt Graphs provides these predefined themes, which you can use as a basis for
    custom themes:

\table
\header
    \li Theme
    \li Base color
\row
    \li \c QtGreen
    \li Green
\row
    \li \c QtGreenNeon
    \li Neon green
\row
    \li \c MixSeries
    \li A mixture of several color series
\row
    \li \c OrangeSeries
    \li Orange
\row
    \li \c YellowSeries
    \li Yellow
\row
    \li \c BlueSeries
    \li Blue
\row
    \li \c PurpleSeries
    \li Purple
\row
    \li \c GreySeries
    \li Grey
\endtable

Use \c UserDefined to create a custom theme.

    You can also define a custom theme.

    If a graph displays data from several series, you can specify some settings
    for each series. For example, specify different gradients for different
    layers of a 3D graph to make it look more realistic. For an example, see
    \l{Surface Graph Gallery}.

    See \l{GraphsTheme} and \l{QGraphsTheme} for details.
*/
